sdata> -- Pins down the genuine REPL-only restriction (originally reported and
sdata> -- documented as doc-only, "1 for now"): with no continuation comma, the
sdata> -- REPL judges a single-line IF's THEN-clause complete the moment it is
sdata> -- typed and submits it for execution immediately -- ELSEIF on the next
sdata> -- line has not been typed yet at that point, so it is parsed as a new,
sdata> -- unrelated top-level statement and rejected. Contrast with
sdata> -- if_elseif_batch_no_comma_continuation.cmd (batch mode, same statement
sdata> -- text, no comma, succeeds) and repl_if_single_line_trailing_comma.cmd
sdata> -- (REPL mode, comma added, succeeds).
sdata> LET inlrn=1
sdata> RUN
RUN complete. 1 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> if inlrn then let sample$="Learn"
sdata> elseif 0 then let sample$="Test"
Error: Unrecognized command "elseif" at line  1 — type HELP for a list of commands
sdata> run
RUN complete. 1 records and 2 variables processed.
sdata> quit
